# Triumph 2500 four-door saloon, 1969-1977.
#
# The 2.5-litre six in the same Mk2 shell as the 2000: same body, same 2.690 m
# wheelbase, same glazing. Sold in Britain as the 2.5 PI (1969-1975), the 2500 TC
# (1974-1977) and the 2500 S (1975-1977). The body was inherited from the 2000
# Mk2 master rather than rebuilt; the grille badge and trim distinguish it.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triumph_2000
# https://triumph2000register.co.uk/the-cars/technical-specifications/
#
# Dimensions 4.630 x 1.690 x 1.420 m, wheelbase 2.690 m, identical to the 2000
# Mk2 because it is the same shell. Mirrors take the modelled width to 1.980 m.
#
# Colours are Triumph's own paint names from the Register's list of genuine
# finishes: Damson, Saffron, French Blue and White. As with the 2000 Mk2, the
# Register does not allocate each colour to a mark and year, so the individual
# intro and retire months are road-presence dates rather than paint evidence.
# Weights damson 3, white 3, saffron 2, frenchblue 2, total 10, provisional
# pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 166 km/h, the period Motor Sport figure for a 1974 UK 2500 TC manual.
# Comfort 88/462, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 88: a little more comfortable than the
# 2000 because of the smoother six. Classes 1,2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence: October 1969 intro, retires staggered 1986-1989.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/triumph-2500.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/triumph-2500.dae (60 objects). References:
# citycars/references/triumph-2500/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Recorded limitations: the pack has no profile and no rear view — all four
# photographs are front three-quarters — so the shell comes entirely from the Mk2
# master and the photographs supply only the nose, badge and trim. Boot badge
# placement is therefore unverified. At 128 px the 2500 is deliberately almost
# indistinguishable from the 2000 Mk2, as the real cars were.

obj=citycar
name=Triumph2500(Damson)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1969
intro_month=10
retire_year=1989
retire_month=6
speed=166
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=88
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=462

